# Angular Standalone Components & Modern Syntax

## Standalone Components
- **ALL new components MUST be standalone** - we are progressively moving from modules-based Angular to standalone system for future Angular version updates
- Use `standalone: true` in component decorator
- Import dependencies directly in the component's `imports` array
- Example structure:
```typescript
@Component({
    standalone: true,
    imports: [CommonModule, TranslateModule, ButtonModule],
    selector: 'app-component-name',
    templateUrl: './component-name.component.html',
    styleUrls: ['./component-name.component.scss'],
})
```

## Modern Angular Syntax
- **Use new control flow syntax instead of structural directives:**
  - Replace `*ngIf` with `@if()`
  - Replace `*ngFor` with `@for()`
  - Replace `*ngSwitch` with `@switch()`
  - Example:
    ```html
    <!-- OLD - do not use -->
    <div *ngIf="condition">Content</div>
    <div *ngFor="let item of items">{{ item.name }}</div>

    <!-- NEW - use this -->
    @if (condition) {
        <div>Content</div>
    }
    @for (item of items; track item.id) {
        <div>{{ item.name }}</div>
    }

    <!-- With else -->
    @if (isLoading) {
        <p-progressSpinner></p-progressSpinner>
    } @else {
        <div>Content loaded</div>
    }
    ```

## Signals
Use Angular signals for reactive state:

```typescript
// Simple signal
protected loaded = signal(false);

// Computed signal (derived state)
protected readonly isFeatureEnabled = computed(() => {
    const data = this.service.data$();
    return data?.feature === true;
});

// Reading signals in template
@if (loaded()) {
    <div>Content</div>
}
```

## Dependency Injection
- **Prioritize new inject() syntax** over constructor injection
- Place all injected services at the top of the class
- Use `private readonly` for services
- Example:
```typescript
export class MyComponent {
    private readonly router = inject(Router);
    private readonly translate = inject(TranslateService);
    private readonly dataService = inject(DataService);

    // ... rest of component
}
```
